  ],
  "text": "Sharks are older than trees. By about fifty million years. A forest feels like the oldest thing you can stand inside. It is not. Sharks had already been going four hundred million years when the first tree grew. They are older than the rings around Saturn. Older than the North Star. Older than Mount Everest. They are not primitive. They just solved the problem extremely early. Teeth on a conveyor belt. Lose one and the next rolls forward into place. Skin that is not scales at all but thousands of tiny teeth, which is why it rasps. Four hundred million years with no redesign. Nothing else alive has that record. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
